Third-party components used by the plotter
==========================================

Qt 6 (Core, Gui, Qml, Quick, Network, Sql, OpenGL, Quick Controls)
  License: LGPL-3.0 (full text: https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html)
  Source: https://download.qt.io (installed with aqtinstall, version 6.8.3)
  Linked dynamically, unmodified, so it can be replaced by another build of the same Qt 6 version.

maplibre-native-qt (core library only, libQMapLibre.so)
  License: BSD-2-Clause
  Source: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-qt (commit pinned in scripts/build-maplibre-qt.sh)
  Built from source by scripts/build-maplibre-qt.sh. Only src/core is built. Its LGPL-3.0 QML
  bindings (Qt Location plugin, src/location) are not built, so they are not part of the plotter.
  The rows below are what the built library compiles in or includes (from
  docs/plotter/spike-findings.md).

MapLibre Native (inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: BSD-2-Clause
  Source: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native

ICU 61.1 (vendored subset, inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: Unicode / ICU licence

nunicode (inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: MIT

parsedate, from curl (inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: curl licence (MIT-style)

csscolorparser (inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: MIT

maplibre-tile-spec C++ (mlt-cpp, inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: MIT or Apache-2.0, at your option (vendor/maplibre-tile-spec/README.md: "All code is dual
  licensed under Apache License v2.0 and MIT license, at your option"; texts in its LICENSE-MIT and
  LICENSE-APACHE).
  Its LICENSE-CC0 (CC0 1.0 Universal, public domain dedication) covers that project's documentation
  and specification content, not the code that is built.
  Source: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-tile-spec

FastPFOR (inside libQMapLibre.so)
  License: Apache-2.0

Header-only code compiled into libQMapLibre.so:
